{"title":"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 22","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/0/580c2665c787b2d05326c611413de6c2395fe05c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2 \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are the roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/a/6ca34279195a96c9295ae2c7e1776fc1e36c5f8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0 + a_1x + a_2x^2 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"156\" height=\"17\" />, then the equality \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/1/f81c1640813cc192adc83708c0aca24fe50782f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0 + a_1x + a_2x^2 = a_0\\left (1 - \\frac {x}{r} \\right ) \\left (1 - \\frac {x}{s} \\right )$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"302\" height=\"33\" /> holds: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/2/d520a9601f89db7f7ce9ed4a672f7fec1840fb5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\text{for all values of }x, a_0\\neq 0 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) }\\ \\text{for all values of }x \\\\ \\textbf{(C) }\\ \\text{only when }x = 0 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) }\\ \\text{only when }x = r \\text{ or }x = s \\\\ \\textbf{(E) }\\ \\text{only when }x = r \\text{ or }x = s, a_0 \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"58\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/5/ee5c7c921b3334f6ecf58c241eeea42acf0ce71e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> cannot be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/0/580c2665c787b2d05326c611413de6c2395fe05c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2 \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"17\" />, so the polynomial can take non-zero values when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/b/34b671ab48de5392b8ddbd64c268ab86395fa0f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" /> and thereby not satisfy the equation. Expanding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/c/bac0c95eebece3a8c4dc1a34b7ea4bf6d2818daf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0(1-\\frac{x}{r})(1-\\frac{x}{s})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"139\" height=\"34\" /> gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/9/95989f0235daea082258b46fdfe4be8f4b3fb14a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0(1-\\frac{x}{r}-\\frac{x}{s}+\\frac{x^2}{rs})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"159\" height=\"41\" />. Using <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Vieta%27s_formulas\" title=\"Vieta&#39;s formulas\">Vieta's formulas</a>, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/c/ddc14650ee70a7c632de8637f315f92f9fdf50e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$rs=\\frac{a_0}{a_2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"64\" height=\"37\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/9/eb92d5ea103ad62183a89b8435009bee25101d4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0=a_2rs$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"13\" />. Plugging this into the expanded right hand side of the given equation, we see that that side equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/e/dae8667eca27055d0233fdc343c979f55231bade.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0-a_2(r+s)x+a_2x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"179\" height=\"21\" />. Using Vieta's formulas again, we equate this expression to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/8/ce8a0fd7bef1564bee98672b64911f253e68857b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0+a_1x+a_2x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"126\" height=\"20\" />, which is the left hand side of the given equation. Thus, as long as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/6/026d01d3f2600a7e756cb88c0a4e32d752279c4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0 \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" />, the equation holds for all values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. This fact corresponds with answer choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/2/af2b0029c8dba2791d55316fb5ea2a7afeea77d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{\\textbf{(A)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"42\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME\" title=\"1965 AHSME\">1965 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1965 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1965\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b